Author: Hieu31 <hzcay1125@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 05:45:39 2026 +0700

    feat: n8n-style integration packages and app triggers (chat-trigger P3)

    Replace the generic trigger.app / chat.reply design with integration
    packages configured entirely in the UI.

    - libs/apps: package contract (credential types, trigger nodes with
      checkExists/create/delete/handle, action nodes), PackageRegistry,
      Webhook and Facebook Messenger packages
    - Catalog sync at startup writes package node and credential types
    - Generic OAuth2 credentials (user's own App ID / Secret) with
      /api/oauth2/auth and /callback; Meta OAuth via .env removed
    - Webhook endpoints /api/webhooks/:id scoped per node or per credential;
      every matching listener runs
    - Active switch: activate/deactivate register and remove webhooks;
      publishing while active switches listeners to the new version
    - Dynamic options (loadOptions) and "Listen for test event"
    - Frontend: Active toggle, OAuth2 credential form, Page picker, webhook
      URL and test event panel
    - Migration rewritten: workflows.active, webhook_endpoints, workflow_triggers
    - E2E runs on its own BullMQ prefix (BULLMQ_PREFIX)

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

